Looking at the folds: the first fold at angle α = 70° turns the strip so the two legs of the "∧" meet at an angle of 180° − 2α = 40°. The second fold (along the direction of one leg) keeps this 40° angle between the two layer directions. The third fold reflects the packet but preserves the angle between the layers; in the final symmetric position, the two arms open downward, and the angle β between them (measured through the bottom) is the supplement of the 40° angle between the strip directions:

β = 180° − (180° − 2α) = 2α = 140°.

\boxed{A}
